KayaMo is a Personal Growth OS. This repository is the **web app**: kayamo.fit,
desktop-first with a phone layout. The assistant is named **Lis**.

Market is **global**, English by default (owner override, 2026-09-14). Filipino
food is one cuisine among many. Native bundle identifiers, stored meal-slot
identifiers and nutrition provenance keep their existing values.

## Layout — put code in the right place

- `src/`         — routes, navigation, composition. Next.js 16 App Router.
- `packages/features` — screen logic, data hooks, layout-neutral components.
- `packages/db` `core` `food` `ai` `offline` `ui` `config` — shared logic.

There is no `apps/` directory here, and no turbo. `src/` is the app.

Packages never import from `src/`. `src/` never reaches into package internals;
it imports declared package exports. A formula or a resolver under `src/` is a
bug. A screen implemented twice is a bug.

`packages/`, `supabase/` and `data/` are **owned by this repository**. They were
forked from `../kayamo-mobile` on 2026-09-18 and are no longer synced. See
AGENTS.md.

## Non-negotiable

- Never call an LLM without a Zod schema on the output.
- Never write nutrition data without `source` and `confidence`.
- The LLM extracts text and quantities. Nutrition numbers come from the
  resolver cascade in @kayamo/food, never from the model.
- Every AI-created entry is editable by the user. Lis proposes; the user confirms.
- Stored data is not automatically AI-readable.
- Offline first: writes go to IndexedDB via @kayamo/offline, then sync.
- Store UTC, render in the user's timezone. Respect their custom day
  boundary (night shift) — never assume midnight, and never assume Asia/Manila.
- Calorie floors (1200F / 1500M) are enforced in code, not prompts.
- Banned vocabulary anywhere in prompts or UI copy: cheat, guilty, earned,
  burn it off, bad food, sinful.
- Health data never appears in logs or error reports.
- Never modify a test to make it pass. Fix the code, or tell me the test
  is wrong and why. Changing a test because the *product decision* changed is
  allowed, and the commit must say so.
- The service-role Supabase client is never imported into a "use client" file.
- All LLM calls route through @kayamo/ai `router.ts`.

## Conventions

- pnpm workspaces. TypeScript strict. No `any`.
- Add a dependency to the package that uses it, not to the root.
- Money in PHP only where a stored price already is; there is no billing yet.

## Commit messages

Describe the change and why. No chapter numbers: the build guide is archived at
`docs/archive/build/` and its `chNN` scheme no longer tracks the work. Reference a document under
`docs/audits/` or `docs/RELEASE.md` when a commit closes something recorded there.
